# THE WOOD (THE MAZE), SLAB 2 — 32 rooms: the band widens, two more cores.
#
# Slab 1 proved the mechanism. This grows it: the honest lattice gains a
# northern and a southern row (so the wood is 5 rows deep instead of 3), two
# more thresholds at its far corners, and TWO more lying cores behind them.
#
# THE CORE PATTERN, now formalised. Each core is 8 rooms in a ring, and every
# room's four exits are assigned by fixed offsets around that ring:
#     north -> +1     east -> +3     south -> +5     west -> +7
# That guarantees the design law with no eyeballing: a -north-> a+1, and that
# room's south goes to a+6, never back to a. Same for every other pair. Every
# room keeps all four compass points, so no direction ever answers "there is no
# way east from here" and gives the trick away.
#
# Two exits per core are replaced with SPILLS back onto the honest band, at
# rooms nowhere near the threshold you entered by.

!region wood

# ---- attachments: the slab-1 rooms that gain a door --------------------------

## the-birch-edge | attachment
!existing
> north the-wind-shorn-edge

## the-holly-brake | attachment
!existing
